 "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["backoff_retry", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379829, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q3Wtw9ME9hFKMhkmsYMLLB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 384843, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` was rounding half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. With half-up, `2.665` became `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\n<br>\n\nThis changes how payments-service rounds amounts that land exactly on a half-cent, so some results will now come out one cent lower than before.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Fx8BUEoqNzU7okyn9Bki6G", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Bsm8FsT4z1o8kJ75qk2122", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JS5RzgGVE3MSY7N9gdhBmK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RwWfbFUpnkh71NVXJSdTsq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-round